            <ArticleTitle>Metabolic profil in a group of obese Moroccan children enrolled in schools in the city of Rabat.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>377</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2014.19.377.3630</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">To determine the metabolic profile in a group of obese children in Morocco.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The BMI, the waist circumference, the blood pressure and metabolic parameters in 73 children (37 obese and 36 normal) were compared.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">80% of obese children had abdominal obesity (p &lt;0.0001). For systolic blood pressure among children who have a higher value than the 95th percentile, 85.7% were obese and 14.3% children are normal children. For diastolic blood pressure, 83.34% of obese children had higher diastolic blood pressure values in the 95th percentile and 16.6% of normal children have a higher value than the 95th percentile (p=0.013). No obese child had hyperglycemia. The prevalence of metabolic syndrome was 21.6%.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Obesity is number one risk of cardiovascular disease for children. Early detection can help for an appropriate care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
